        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "@echasnovski, sorry for not being clear in my explanation; I really struggle to express my ideas (writing and speaking).\r\n\r\nThe feature I am asking for is to have an option to control whether commenting/uncommenting should apply a space (padding) after (and before in some cases) the comment delimiter(s).\r\n\r\nThe explanation about the types of comments was intended to kinda justify this feature request: if the user wants to comment code in a way that differs from how they write doc comments, they are able to do so.\r\n\r\nWorth mentioning that maybe the user would like to control both left and right padding, so I thought something like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nrequire'mini.comment'.setup{\r\n  padding = {\r\n    left = false, -- No space after start delimiter.\r\n    right = true, -- With space before end delimiter.\r\n  },\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI hope that I was clear this time. Thanks for the attention!",
