        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I understand this better now, thanks.\r\n\r\n> The explanation about the types of comments was intended to kinda justify this feature request: if the user wants to comment code in a way that differs from how they write doc comments, they are able to do so.\r\n\r\nBut not really this part. How are they able to do so? If by manually adding/removing padding, then how it is different from the current situation?\r\n\r\nHowever, I think adding a boolean option to not trim whitespace from comment parts (as is done now) is reasonable, though. Your case can then be supported by setting appropriate 'commentstring' (like `--%s` or `<!--%s-->`).",
