        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "In the case of the user, they would be able to differentiate by writing doc comments in a way that differs from the options established by `'commentstring'` in conjunction with the proposed options for `mini.comment`.\r\n\r\nFor instance, if a user write doc comments with padding, they would be able to set a proper `'commentstring'` that does not make use of padding and also configure `mini.comment` to do not add padding when dealing with comments.\r\n\r\nI'm having some trouble to change `'commentstring'`. Using `:verbose setl comentstring?` it shows that `'commentstring'` is last set from Lua. Seems that it gets automatically reset after I changing it. Due to that, I cannot properly test the behavior of `mini.comment`.\r\n\r\nI will figure out what is happening before trying to check if currently `mini.comment` works as expected with a proper `'commentstring'`.",
