        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks again for suggestion! I wanted to make this behavior behind an option, but it never had enough priority to me.\r\n\r\nThis should in `main` branch now under `config.options.pad_comment_parts`. Your use case can be achieved with `require('mini.comment').setup({ options = { pad_comment_parts = false } })` and setting proper 'commentstring' option per file type. It can be used with `FileType` autocommand like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd(\r\n  'FileType',\r\n  {\r\n    pattern = 'lua',\r\n    callback = function() vim.bo.commentstring = '--%s' end,\r\n  }\r\n)\r\n```\r\n\r\nI'd suggest using 'after/ftplugin' for this: create 'lua.lua' file in '.config/nvim/after/ftplugin' directory (possibly create it too) with content `vim.bo.commentstring = '--%s'`.\r\n\r\n**Edit**: rename `pad_comment_leaders` to a more appropriate `pad_comment_parts`.",
